  "evidence": "TEXT_E: commits to leaving the single market and customs union with immigration controlled to the tens of thousands; at least £8bn extra for the NHS; 1.5m homes by 2022; low taxes and an industrial strategy; strong defence and security (retain Trident); an energy price cap for consumers. TEXT_G: seeks Single Market membership for Scotland and a post‑Brexit independence choice; increases NHS Scotland budget by £2bn; devolves immigration and protects EU citizens’ rights; anti‑austerity welfare reforms; 50,000 affordable homes in Scotland; scrap Trident.",
